# Orchestrator env — documents the SHAPE only. Never commit real secrets.
#
# Local (Steps 1–5): no secrets needed — agents run via the ambient Claude Code
# auth (OAuth token) already present in the environment.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Step 6 — Railway box (set these as Railway service variables, NOT in git):
#
# code-server auth (REQUIRED — the box refuses to start without one of these):
#   PASSWORD=                 # a strong random password for code-server, OR
#   HASHED_PASSWORD=          # preferred: argon2 hash (so plaintext isn't in env)
#
# Private access via Tailscale (RECOMMENDED — keeps code-server off the public net):
#   TS_AUTHKEY=               # a Tailscale auth key you generate (ephemeral/reusable)
#   TS_HOSTNAME=orchestrator-box   # optional; the box's name on your tailnet
#
# Volume + paths (defaults shown; override only if you change the mount):
#   DATA_DIR=/data            # Railway persistent volume mount point
#   APP_DIR=/app              # baked working tree (repo) inside the image
#
# Subscription auth is interactive: run `claude auth login` inside code-server
# AFTER lockdown. There is NO API key — do not set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY on the box.
